# Claude Code tooling and temp files
# NOTE: CLAUDE.md is deliberately NOT ignored. A bare `claude.md` used to sit in the
# NUnit block above and, because core.ignorecase is true on Windows, it silently
# untracked the project's own operating instructions - unversioned, unrecoverable, and
# absent from a fresh clone. If you are re-adding an ignore for Claude files, scope it
# to .claude/ and leave CLAUDE.md tracked.
.claude/
.tmp_nat.json

# Vendored ScriptHookVDotNet nightly (build input, fetched by tools\fetch-shvdn.ps1).
# Not source, and ~11 MB of binaries per nightly bump.
external/

# Debug logs and generated triage artifacts (drive-assist and menu/phone)
driveassist-*.log
menulog-*.log
triage/
tools/log-index.json
tools/menulog-index.json

# Tooling scratch: cached game files + generated suggestion dumps
tools/_cache/
tools/_align_suggestions.json

# Map-data build inputs and archives (large / regenerable via CodeWalker)
navmesh_exports/
*.7z

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Regenerated by tools\build-modelnames.py on every run: ~57k rows, 1.5 MB, and derived
# entirely from the shipped .tsv.gz. It is a worklist for modelnames-overrides.json,
# not a source. The overrides file IS tracked.
tools/modelnames-review.txt

# Runtime settings copies (real file lives in Documents\Rockstar Games\GTA V\ModSettings)
gta11ySettings.json

# Packaged testing releases (built by hand, not tracked)
dist/

# Reference material for a DIFFERENT game (Sleeping Dogs: Definitive Edition Lua
# modding API, mirrored from sneakyevil.gitbook.io 2026-07-24). 15.9 MB / 108 files,
# nothing in this repo references it, and it would roughly double the git history.
# Kept on disk as a worked example of an accessible script-API surface; just not tracked.
sleeping-dogs-de-script-api/
